    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a for-profit public company headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, trading under the ticker LUMN with CIK 0000018926. According to its website, it provides secure networking, edge cloud and AI-ready infrastructure over a global fiber network, and it describes itself as the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy. The company says its fiber footprint reaches across markets and reduces latency where it matters, supporting real-time performance.\n\nThe site presents customer examples rather than a product list. It says its programmable, consumption-based network gives the New York Yankees real-time scalability and resiliency through diverse 100G paths and automatic failover. It says it built a private, low-latency network for Prometheus Hyperscale designed for heavy AI workloads, and that Prometheus anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady. It also cites American Family Care, which it says was scaling across 26 states, and Arctic Glacier, where it says built-in automation replaced manual operations.\n\nThe profile data records law exposure in Louisiana with a count of 57. No specific products or MCP servers are listed for the company.",
